;; X3 (gym-v2 §3 Group II) — discover-then-filter-and-sum over a SEEDED
;; dataset, forking nothing. A cold agent (never told the :my.expense/* kind)
;; is asked a category-scoped total: it must DISCOVER the kind, filter to
;; :dining, and SUM (=106) — WITHOUT minting a parallel spelling for the same
;; shape.
;;
;; SINGLE agent over a SEEDED store (deliberately NOT the old A-logs→B-reads
;; shape): pre-seeded fixtures PLUS an agent re-logging the same week mint
;; DUPLICATE entities (:my.expense/merchant is not an identity attr),
;; doubling dining to 212 and silently corrupting the judge. A controlled
;; memory instrument needs ONE unambiguous dataset, so the rows are seeded and
;; a single cold agent analyses them — the same fix x-category-argmax uses.
;; Discovery + no-fork are preserved: the agent is never told the kind; it
;; must read the seeded rows and must not invent a parallel :my.dining/* or
;; :spend/* spelling. The seeded rows ARE the prior state a session left.
;;
;; Mechanical legs: discovery (op-family), the seeded rows are visible at an
;; EXACT count (a re-log regression shows as 10, RED, not a doubled total),
;; and NO new domain attr was minted (provenance-anchored no-fork). The exact
;; dining total lives ONLY on the judge axis.
;;
;; PAID — refused without {:seon.gym/allow-paid? true} + the provider key.
{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :x3-expense-reuse-and-category-total
 :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "A cold agent, never told the :my.expense/* kind, is asked how much it spent eating out this week. It must discover the kind, filter to :dining, SUM (=106), and reply — over a seeded, unambiguous dataset (no re-log double-count), forking no parallel attr spelling."
 :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
 :seon.gym.scenario/status :active
 :seon.gym.scenario/competency :db-memory
 :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:consults-findings :reuses-schemas
                            :replies-honestly :terminates]
 :seon.gym.scenario/schema-registrations
 [[:my.expense/merchant :string]
  [:my.expense/amount-usd :int]
  [:my.expense/category :keyword]]
 ;; dining = 28+52+26 = 106; transport 40; groceries 73. Total 219.
 :seon.gym.scenario/fixtures
 [{:my.expense/merchant "Thai Place"    :my.expense/amount-usd 28 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Sushi Bar"     :my.expense/amount-usd 52 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Cafe Luna"     :my.expense/amount-usd 26 :my.expense/category :dining}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Shell"         :my.expense/amount-usd 40 :my.expense/category :transport}
  {:my.expense/merchant "Trader Joe's"  :my.expense/amount-usd 73 :my.expense/category :groceries}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/turns
 [{:seon.gym.turn/message "How much did I spend eating out this week?"}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
 [{:seon.gym.predicate/id     :expenses-seeded-visible
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :consults-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?e :where [?e :my.expense/amount-usd _]]
   ;; EXACTLY 5 — a regression that re-introduces the double-count (an agent
   ;; re-logging the seeded week) shows up here as 10, RED, not as a silently
   ;; doubled judge total.
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 5]}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id      :discovery-reads-store-first
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind    :first-eval-matches
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent   :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis    :consults-findings
   ;; Match the TAUGHT alias `db/query` (agent nses alias seon.db :as db;
   ;; the manual teaches db/query, db/entity) AND fully-qualified
   ;; seon.db/query — `\bdb/` hits both (the `.` is a word boundary).
   :seon.gym.predicate/pattern "\\bdb/(query|pull|entity|store-inventory)"}
  ;; NO FORK (generic, provenance-anchored): every agent-domain attr in the
  ;; post-run store is one of the seeded :my.expense/* attrs — the agent
  ;; reused the shape and minted no parallel spelling (e.g. :my.dining/* or
  ;; :spend/*).
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :no-attr-fork-for-the-expense-shape
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :domain-attrs
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :reuses-schemas
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:every-in [":my.expense/merchant"
                                          ":my.expense/amount-usd"
                                          ":my.expense/category"]]}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :replied-to-the-user
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/a]
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?m
                               :in $ ?aid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?aid]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/from ?ag]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/hops ?h]
                               [(pos? ?h)]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :agent-ends-idle
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   ;; idle is DERIVED, never a stored :seon.agent/state datom: an agent is
   ;; idle iff not terminated and owns NO open run (the run's close retracts
   ;; :seon.agent/run → derived :idle). The single agent idle = 1.
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?a
                               :where
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                               (not [?a :seon.agent/terminated-at _])
                               (not-join [?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?a]
                                 [?r :seon.agent.run/status :open])]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 1]}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-dining-total
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent     :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the reply states the dining / eating-out total as 106 USD (allow 105-107 for rounding). FAIL if it reports a different number, sums the wrong category, or includes the gas/grocery spend in the eating-out figure."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "Dining rows: Thai Place 28 + Sushi Bar 52 + Cafe Luna 26 = 106. The non-dining rows (Shell 40 transport, Trader Joe's 73 groceries) must be EXCLUDED. 106 is knowable only by reading the stored rows and filtering on the dining category."}]}
